Coursework report, October 2026: optimisation of MZ77
=====================================================

The report for the task "оптимизировать курсовую работу по
программированию с предыдущих курсов" (discipline «Языки
программирования»), in Russian, built with pdflatex.

  make            report.pdf (latexmk; TeX Live with extsizes, tempora,
                  pgfplots, titlesec, tocloft)
  make data       regenerate data/*.dat from ../../bench/log
  make clean      remove LaTeX's intermediate files

report.pdf is not committed; build it.

Layout
------

  report.tex               title-page fields (\reporttitle, \reportauthor,
                           ...) and the list of chapters
  spbpu-coursework.sty     the layout of coursework_template.docx; the
                           header of the file says which Word setting
                           each part reproduces
  chapters/                one file per chapter, in report order
  data/extract.py          turns bench/log into the tables the charts read
  data/scaling.sh          measures instructions against input size
                           (data/scaling-raw.txt, run on hppavillion)
  pic/                     screenshots; window.png is from the May report

Where the numbers come from
---------------------------

  steps-*.dat     bench/log/MACHINE/steps/steps.txt (cycles, all steps
                  rebuilt and measured back to back)
  profile-*.dat   bench/log/MACHINE/STEP/raw/profile/summary.txt (perf stat
                  on dickens, profiling build -O2 -g)
  perfile-*.dat,  bench/log/MACHINE/STEP/raw/bench.csv (wall clock; only
  wall-*.dat      debian's is quoted, the laptop's clock was unstable)
  paths-*.dat     bench/log/MACHINE/06-avx2/raw/followup/ab-cycles.txt
  scaling-*.dat   data/scaling-raw.txt

Numbers typed into the text and tables come from the same files and
from doc/optimisations/*.md; ../../doc/optimisations/RESULTS.md is the
guide to all of them.

Screenshots to take
-------------------

Every \screenshot in chapters/ shows a framed red placeholder until
pic/NAME.png (or .jpg) exists; then the picture replaces it.  The
placeholder itself says which command to run.  In report order:

  machines        lscpu and gcc --version on both machines, side by side
  base-perfstat   perf stat of the original program on dickens
  base-gprof      gprof flat profile of the original program
  base-perflines  hottest source lines of the original program (perf)
  perf-14         perf stat after #14 (no memmove), next to step 02
  gprof-12        gprof flat profile after #12 (inline bit I/O)
  perf-15         profile summary after #15 (8-byte compare)
  make-pgo        output of make pgo
  match-paths     perf stat cycles with MZ77_MATCH unset, avx2, word
  steps-debian    cat bench/log/debian/steps/steps.txt
  steps-hpp       cat bench/log/hppavillion/steps/steps.txt
  sha256          diff of archives.sha256, baseline against final
  make-check      make check summary
  final-gprof     gprof flat profile of the final program

All the files named there are already in bench/log, so most
screenshots are just 'cat' or 'head' of a committed log in a terminal.
